ction: flips with the sign of q\", and a proton \"(+)\" enters the plate stage on the same line, its path bending down, drawn dashed in full ink (its true deflection, 2.7 μm, is invisible; tag \"proton: 1837 times less, drawn enlarged\"). Revision 2: violet hand tag \"≫ g in this field\" with a pen ring round \"3.5 × 10¹⁵\"; ink hand tag \"same g, every ball\" in the cliff panel; amber hand tag \"sign flips it\" by the proton.\ncalculation layout, with the plate stage small at the right (brackets L and d visible throughout scenes 4 to 6). Task strip: \"Electron enters on the centre line: find the time between the plates.\" Equation strip: \"t = L/v_x\". Givens grouped: \"v_x = 3.0 × 10⁷ m s⁻¹\", \"L = 5.0 cm = 0.050 m\", \"d = 2.0 cm, V = 400 V → E = 2.0 × 10⁴ V m⁻¹\". `AlignedAlgebra`: \"t = 0.050 / 3.0 × 10⁷\"; on \"seconds\" \"= 1.67 × 10⁻⁹ s\" framed. On \"all\" the strobe images' horizontal ticks highlight, tag \"t from the horizontal motion only\"; a chip \"bigger push → longer inside\" fades in and is crossed in red, red hand tag \"only v_x and L set t\". Revision 2: the plate stage at the right fills about 40% of the frame (not a thumbnail), with the L and d brackets in navy; navy hand tag \"cm → m\" with a pen ring round \"0.050 m\".\ncamera continue. Equation strip adds \"y = ½at², a = qE/m\". `AlignedAlgebra`: \"a = (1.602 × 10⁻¹⁹ × 2.0 × 10⁴)/(9.109 × 10⁻³¹) = 3.52 × 10¹⁵ m s⁻²\", \"y = ½ × 3.52 × 10¹⁵ × (1.67 × 10⁻⁹)²\"; on \"millimetres\" \"= 4.89 × 10⁻³ m (4.9 mm), up\" framed. On \"out\" the stage's exit point gets a navy bracket \"y = 4.9 mm\" beside a bracket \"d/2 = 10 mm\", and a tick \"4.9 mm < 10 mm: exits\". Revision 2: violet hand tag \"starts from zero up\" with a pen arrow to \"½at²\"; navy hand tag \"room = half the gap\" by the d/2 bracket.\n\ncamera pull back to 4 px per mm. The beam continues straight from the exit point (no strobe acceleration arrows outside the plates). On \"line\" (first) a tag \"no force: straight (Newton's first la